# Project Agents & AI Assistant Guide

## Overview
This is a React + TypeScript project using the **{{pattern}}** architectural pattern.
All components live under `{{basePath}}/`.

## Directory Structure
{{#if (eq pattern "atomic")}}
```
{{basePath}}/
  components/
    atoms/       — Primitive UI elements (buttons, inputs, icons)
    molecules/   — Composite elements (form fields, cards)
    organisms/   — Complex UI sections (headers, sidebars)
    templates/   — Page layout skeletons
    pages/       — Full page components
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "pages-components")}}
```
{{basePath}}/
  components/    — Reusable UI components
  pages/         — Route-level page components
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "feature-first")}}
```
{{basePath}}/
  features/
    <feature-name>/
      components/   — Feature-specific components
      hooks/        — Feature-specific hooks
      utils/        — Feature-specific utilities
      index.ts      — Public API (re-exports)
  shared/           — Cross-feature shared components
```
{{/if}}

## Scaffolding Commands
Use the rorg CLI to scaffold new components correctly:
{{#if (eq pattern "atomic")}}
```bash
npx rorg atom       # Create an atom
npx rorg molecule   # Create a molecule
npx rorg organism   # Create an organism
npx rorg template   # Create a template
npx rorg page       # Create a page
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "pages-components")}}
```bash
npx rorg component  # Create a reusable component
npx rorg page       # Create a page component
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq pattern "feature-first")}}
```bash
npx rorg feature    # Create a new feature module
npx rorg shared     # Create a shared component
```
{{/if}}

## Component File Structure
Each component directory contains:
```
ComponentName/
  ComponentName.tsx    — Component implementation
  index.ts             — Re-export: export { ComponentName } from './ComponentName'
{{#if separateCss}}  ComponentName.module.css — CSS Module styles{{/if}}
{{#if includeTests}}  ComponentName.test.tsx   — Jest + Testing Library tests{{/if}}
```

## TypeScript Standards
- All components: `React.FC<Props>` with a named interface `{Name}Props`
- Children: typed as `React.ReactNode`
- No `any` types
- Named exports only (no `export default`)

## When Generating Code
1. Always create all files in the component directory
2. Match the exact naming convention (`PascalCase` for components)
3. Include the `index.ts` re-export file
{{#if separateCss}}4. Reference styles via `import styles from './ComponentName.module.css'`{{/if}}
{{#if includeTests}}5. Add a corresponding `.test.tsx` file using `@testing-library/react`{{/if}}
